startDebug(receiver, method, arguments) -> snapshot or error
  Require a native method and its exact argument count; validate typed values.
  Reject a second active session. Retain the method, defining class and arguments.
  Queue execution on the receiver's normal mailbox; reject a full mailbox.

runDebug(session) -> value
  Hold a native evaluator context for this invocation.
  Pause before the first outer statement. Step pauses before the next statement.
  Continue preserves the frame and runs until return, signal or end.
  An uncaught signal pauses at the same statement. Earlier effects remain.
  Apply edited arguments and declared receiver fields only at a pause.
  Replacement Smalltalk evaluates in place of that statement for this invocation.
  Retry repeats the statement. Return supplies a result. Abort ends execution.
  Expire an unattended pause after ten minutes and release the mailbox.

debugCommand(session ID, revision, action, edits, replacement, value) -> snapshot/error
  Validate syntax, field/argument names and Value kinds before accepting.
  Reject stale revisions and nonpaused frames; accept one command per pause.

debugDispatch(selector, JSON request) -> JSON snapshot
  __debugStart:, __debugCommand:, __debugJson are control messages.
  __debugRun: executes in the normal mailbox.
  Snapshots preserve typed arguments/results; these references join pulse tracing.
